  "recommendation": {
    "decision": "Ollama is the v1 serving backend; vLLM stays a documented seam (runtime.py) for dedicated halo-class pools.",
    "basis": "Measured on U1/GB10 2026-10-26, same prompts both sides: Ollama qwen3:8b Q4 41.5/38.8 tok/s short/long, 31/32 ms warm TTFT, 3.9 s cold load, 6.0 GB resident. vLLM 0.32 Qwen3-4B bf16 15.0/14.5 tok/s, 134/142 ms warm TTFT, 357 s first-boot to healthy (Triton JIT for sm_121), 38-39 GiB pre-reserved.",
    "vllm_platform_verdict": "installs and runs on aarch64/sm_121 from stock PyPI wheels (torch 2.13.0+cu130); the blockers are operational, not platform.",
    "not_adopted_because": [
      "357 s first boot dominated by kernel JIT (warm-cache second boot not measured)",
      "pre-reserves 0.32-0.5 of the unified pool at startup and aborts when co-tenants free/claim memory mid-profile (3 failed starts recorded)",
      "~15 tok/s on a half-size 4B bf16 model while Ollama served 85 tok/s on a 26B at the same time"
    ],
    "revisit_when": "a dedicated (non-co-tenant) halo-class unit exists; then re-run bench/bench_vllm.py with the warm Triton cache, --enforce-eager off, higher utilization, and the same weights as the Ollama comparison.",
    "verified_by": "parent agent 2026-10-26: report and JSON read from disk, 27 measurement rows present, independent Ollama spot-check 41.64 tok/s on qwen3:8b (load 2.8 s) matching the 41.5 reported."
  },
